      "message": "The Zephyr way to do this is to create 2 `k_timepoint_t` fields. One for the long press and one for press timeout.\n\n```\npb_press_timeout \u003d sys_timepoint_calc(K_SECONDS(8));\npb_long_press \u003d sys_timepoint_calc(K_SECONDS(4));\n```\n\nYou then test using\n\n```\n   if (!sys_timepoint_expired(pb_press_timeout)) {\n       if (sys_timepoint_expired(pb_long_press)) {\n           /* Shutdown if AP is on */\n```",
